# RaceDay API (PROG6212 POE – Part 2)ASP.NET Core 8 Web API for the RaceDay system. It uses Entity Framework Core (Code-First) withith two roles (Organiser and Participant), Swaggerith two roles (Organiser and Participant), Swagger, xUnit unitCI](ts and a GitHub Actions CI/CD pipeline.[![CI](https://github.com/<your-userna)e>/<yous)## Setup and run instructions**Prereq/actions)## Setup and run instructions**Prereq/actions)## Setup and run instructions**Prerequisites:** .NET 8 SDK, Visual Studio 2022 (AS SQL Server Locan` in Visual Studio.2. Check the connection string inn Visual Studio.2. Check the connection string in `RaceDay.Api/appsettings.jsonconnection string in `RaceDay.Api/appsettings.json`. It defaults to LocalDB with a database called `irst model. In Create the database from the Code `RaceDay.Api` as the default project, nsole, with `RaceDay.Api` as the default project, run:   ```   Add-Migration InitialCreate   Update-Database   ```   (If no migration exists, the API creates the schema automatically on first start.)4. Run the API with the green Run button or `dotnet run --project RaceDay.Api`. Swagger opennit tests with ceshost:5080/swagger`.5. Run the unit tests with Test Explorer or `dotnet test RaceDay.sln`.**Using Swagger:** call `POST /api/auth/register`, then `POST /api/authautgin`. Swagger UI then sends the session cookie automatically with every other request.## The two roles| Role | What they can do ||------|------------------|| **Organiser** | Create, update and delete their own events. Define age or distance categories for their events. View all enrolments for their events. Capture finish times and finishing positions. View and update their own profile. View events and categories. || **Participant** | Register and log in. View and update their own profile selecting a category. Viees. Enrol in an event by selecting a category. View and withdraw their own enrolments. View their own results. |- Organiser functionality returns **403 Forbidden** for a Participant, and Participant functionality returns **403** for an Organiser.- Requests from users who are not logged in return **401 Unauthorized**.- An Organiser can only manage the events they created.- Role selection at registration is controlled: if `Registration:OrganiserCode` is set in configuration, only people who supply that code can register as an Organiser.## Endpoints| Method | Route | Access ||--------|-------|--------|| POST | /api/auth/register | Public || POST | /api/auth/login | Public || POST | /api/auth/logout | Logged  | /a| GET, PUT | /api/profile | Logged in || GET | /api/events, /api/eventsnts, /api/events/{id} | Organiser (owner) || GET | /api/events/{eventId}/categories |wner) || GET | /api/events/{eventId}/categories | Logged in || POST | /api/events/{eventId}/categories | Organiser (owner) || DELETE | /api/categories/{id} | Organiser (owner) || POST | /api/events/{eventId}/enrolments | Participant || GET | /api/enrolments/mine | Participant || DELETE | /api/enrolments/{id} | Participant (own) || GET | /api/events/{eventId}/enrolments | Organiser (owner) || POST, GET | /api/events/{eventId}/results | Organiser (owner) || GET | /api/results/mine | Participant |## Security- Passwords are hashed with BCrypt. Plain-text passwords are never stored.- Session state (user id and role) is held in a signed, HttpOnly cookie that expires aftethorize(Roles = ..activity.- Role checks use `[Authorize(Roles = ...)]`, and ownership checks stop one Organiser editing another Organiser's events.## Unit testsThe `RaceDay.Tests` project uses xUnit and runs the real API in memory. It covers success and failure cases for:- User registration and login, including duplicate emails, wrong passwords and hashed password storage- Event management by Organisers, including editing another Organiser's event- Role rejection in both directions (Participant on Organiser features and the reverse)- Event enrolments being recorded correctly, and duplicate or invalid enrolments being rejected- Capturing and viewing results## CI/CD`.github/workflows/ci.yml` builds the project and runsocs/cunit tests on every push.![Green build](docs/ci-green-build.png)## Demo videoYouTube (unlisted): <paste your YouTube link here>
